diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..663de5664d620b7da946e4423ff9021ca8372ead
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+I kept all existing network weights and biases. I added three ReLU units to each original hidden layer and replaced the output with a ReLU maximum construction.
+
+Let f be the original logit, e the error rate, and t the critical-tier flag. The added units compute q = ReLU(e - 0.7), r = ReLU(0.7 - e), and c = ReLU(1 - t). The new output is ReLU(f - g) + g = max(f, g), where g = q - r - c = e - 0.7 - (1 - t).
+
+For critical alerts, g is positive exactly when e > 0.7. For other alerts, g is at most -0.7. Thus the new decision is exactly the original decision OR the required override. At e = 0.7, a previously negative logit becomes zero and still does not escalate.
+
+The original computation remains intact. The added branch uses neither tone nor impact nor region, so it preserves both earlier corrections. Some nonpositive logits change, but every decision outside the override remains the same. No weights were trained or fitted.

